            <h2>FAQ</h2>

            <h3>1. How much does a Holland America cruise usually cost? </h3>
            <p>Holland America cruise prices vary based on destination, cabin type, and travel season. Shorter cruises in inside cabins can start at a few hundred dollars per person, while longer or luxury voyages may cost significantly more. </p>
            <h3> 2. Does Holland America offer all-inclusive cruise packages? </h3>
            <p>Holland America is not fully all-inclusive, but guests can upgrade with the “Have It All” package, which includes shore excursions, specialty dining, Wi-Fi, and a beverage package for added convenience and value. </p>
            <h3>3. Are gratuities included in Holland America cruise fares? </h3>
            <p>Gratuities are generally charged separately on Holland America cruises. However, the cruise line sometimes runs promotions where gratuities are included in the overall cruise fare. </p>
            <h3>4. What is Club Orange on Holland America cruises? </h3>
            <p>Club Orange is an optional upgrade that provides priority check-in, priority tendering, exclusive dining, and other perks. Availability and pricing depend on the specific sailing and ship. </p>
            <h3>5. Are Holland America cruises suitable for budget travelers? </h3>
            <p>Yes, Holland America offers options for budget-conscious travelers, especially when booking inside or ocean-view cabins and traveling during less busy seasons. </p>


